# Live FRM server (read-only)

A **live FicsIt Remote Monitoring (FRM)** instance is available on the group's home network for development and verification. Agents may query it any time for real response shapes and example data.

## Endpoint

| Field | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Host | `192.168.178.42` |
| Port | `8889` |
| Base URL | `http://192.168.178.42:8889` |
| Auth | None required (no `X-FRM-Authorization` on this deployment) |

Env vars for integration tests: `FRM_TEST_HOST=192.168.178.42`, `FRM_TEST_PORT=8889` (see `.env.example`).

## READ ONLY — mandatory

- **Only** `GET` requests to **Read** endpoints under spec §4.1.
- **Never** call `docs/frm-docs/.../json/Write/*` endpoints (`setSwitches`, `sendChatMessage`, `createPing`, etc.).
- **Never** POST, PUT, PATCH, or DELETE to the FRM server.
- **Never** change game state, send chat, or trigger in-game actions via FRM.

FactoryMate v1 is read-only against FRM. Violating this rule is a hard stop.

## Polled endpoints (all verified reachable)

**Fast poll (§4.1):**

```text
GET /getPlayer
GET /getPower
GET /getSchematics
GET /getSpaceElevator
GET /getResearchTrees
GET /getTrains
GET /getVehicles
```

**Slow poll (§4.1):**

```text
GET /getProdStats
GET /getResourceSink
GET /getFactory
GET /getDrone
GET /getDoggo
```

## When to use live FRM

| Use case | Action |
| --- | --- |
| M2 struct design / parse tests | `curl` live endpoint, compare to `docs/frm-docs/` adoc |
| M3/M9 field validation | Capture response snippet, save to `backend/testdata/frm/` if useful offline |
| `getFactory` `building_type` mapping (§4.1) | Query live `getFactory`, extract real `ClassName` values |
| Elevator phase matching (M3.1) | Query live `getSpaceElevator` for current save state |
| Integration tests | `go test -tags=integration` when `FRM_TEST_HOST` is set |

Prefer **JSON fixtures** in `backend/testdata/frm/` for unit tests so CI does not depend on network. Refresh fixtures from live FRM when structs change or adoc drifts.

## Example

```bash
curl -sS "http://192.168.178.42:8889/getPower" | jq .
curl -sS "http://192.168.178.42:8889/getSpaceElevator" | jq .
```

Large responses (`getSchematics`, `getFactory`): pipe to a file locally; do not commit multi‑MB captures unless trimmed for fixture use.

